      ],
      "source": "https://www.knowway.org/en/discover-the-charming-coastal-town-of-nanakuli-hawaii",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nanakuli hosts one of the oldest Hawaiian Home Land Divisions, established by the 1921 Native Hawaiian Homes Commission Act.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/N%C4%81n%C4%81kuli%2C_Hawaii",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Three Nanakuli public schools—Nanakuli High & Intermediate, Nānā I Ka Pono, and Nanakuli Elementary—are uniquely located on Hawaiian Home Lands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
